gflags 2.3.1 replaced include_prefix = "gflags" with includes = ["gen"].
Both expose <gflags/gflags.h> to cc dependents, but only the former routes
headers through _virtual_includes artifacts in CcInfo compilation contexts,
which TAPA's header_extractor (bazel/header_extractor.bzl) relies on to
stage runtime headers for tapacc and the Vitis HLS jobs.
--- bazel/gflags.bzl
+++ bazel/gflags.bzl
@@ -104,6 +104,6 @@
         srcs = srcs,
         copts = copts,
         linkopts = linkopts,
         visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
-        includes = ["gen"],
+        strip_include_prefix = "gen",
     )
